Q3 — Eligibility Decision

A study has the following information:

subject <- c("SUB001","SUB002","SUB003","SUB004","SUB005")

age <- c(17,25,62,45,70)

weight <- c(55,60,72,48,80)

A patient can participate in the study only if they:

are at least 18 years old
AND weigh at least 50 kg

The study coordinator wants the program to classify each patient as either:

"Eligible"

or

"Not Eligible"

For example, the result should correspond to:

SUB001 → Not Eligible
SUB002 → Eligible
...

Design your own function to perform this classification.

Q4 — Risk Classification 🔥

A clinical team wants to classify patients according to age and weight.

subject <- c("SUB001","SUB002","SUB003","SUB004","SUB005",
             "SUB006","SUB007","SUB008")

age <- c(25,62,48,71,35,55,67,60)

weight <- c(58,74,63,81,69,72,79,76)

The rules are:

High Risk → age ≥ 60 AND weight ≥ 75
Moderate Risk → age ≥ 60 OR weight ≥ 75
Low Risk → everyone else

The output should classify each patient.

Don't just return the high-risk patients. The function should produce a risk classification for every subject.

Q5 — 🧠 Final Challenge: Study Review

You are given:

subject <- c("SUB001","SUB002","SUB003","SUB004","SUB005",
             "SUB006","SUB007","SUB008","SUB009","SUB010")

age <- c(25,62,48,71,35,55,67,60,42,73)

